(1043, 'chimney', 1, '/tʃɪmni/', 'A vertical tube or hollow column used to emit environmentally polluting gaseous and solid matter (including but not limited to by-products of burning carbon or hydrocarbon based fuels); a flue.', '煙囪', 'https://api.dictionaryapi.dev/media/pronunciations/en/chimney-us.mp3', 1, '2026-06-01 14:48:14'),
