(3145, 'hypocrisy', 1, '/hɪˈpɒkɹəsi/', 'The contrivance of a false appearance of virtue or goodness, while concealing real character or inclinations, especially with respect to religious and moral beliefs; hence in general sense, dissimulation, pretence, sham.', '偽善、虛偽', 'https://dictionaryapi.dev/hypocrisy', 1, '2026-06-01 14:48:14'),
