(3420, 'jam', 1, '/ˈdʒæːm/', 'A sweet mixture of fruit boiled with sugar and allowed to congeal. Often spread on bread or toast or used in jam tarts.', '果醬、擁擠、卡住', 'https://api.dictionaryapi.dev/media/pronunciations/en/jam-uk.mp3', 1, '2026-06-01 14:48:14'),
